      "writtenOn": "2025-02-05T14:24:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Documentation of the UNKNOWN_RUNTIME_ERROR is \"There was a runtime error while running microdroid manager.\" Did you mean `STOP_REASON_MICRODROID_PAYLOAD_VERIFICATION_FAILED`?\n\nOverall, we should strive to never return the UNKNOWN_RUNTIME_ERROR, since it doesn\u0027t provide any addoitional context when looking at the dashboard.\n\nIn this case, I think that PAYLOAD_VERIFICATION_FAILED is the correct response - SK detected a downgrade and rejected the payload.\n\nIf some of the SK errors are retriable, then microdroid_manager should handle the retry, not the payload.",
